cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GEMS-RAG: structure-aware multimodal retrieval over the MUTCD"
message: "If you use this software, the MUTCD-150 benchmark, or these results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Azad
    given-names: Hannan
repository-code: "https://github.com/hannanazad/gemsrag"
abstract: >-
  GEMS-RAG is a structure-aware multimodal retrieval-augmented generation
  system for the Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices (MUTCD, 11th
  Edition). It encodes the manual's section hierarchy, its normative typology
  of Standard, Guidance, Option and Support provisions, and its internal
  cross-reference graph, then uses all three as retrieval priors alongside
  hybrid dense and sparse text search and late-interaction visual retrieval
  over page images and figure crops. The repository includes the MUTCD-150
  benchmark of 150 annotated questions, a twelve-configuration model
  comparison, a six-condition leave-one-out ablation study, and a comparison
  against BM25, GraphRAG and PaperQA.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - multimodal retrieval
  - knowledge graph
  - technical standards
  - MUTCD
  - benchmark
